title: Short Circuit
text: Red in, red out, and nothing past the machine. It cannot be unplugged, but no machine can bear to hear its own answer.
trick: the fixed complementor must go dark while red still reaches it: send its cyan output right round the board and merge it back onto its own input with a splitter. Its input changes, it contradicts itself and shuts down, and the whole loop goes dark. A red filter that seems pointless protects the second complementor on the splitter arm, which the surge would also shut down
motif: circuit board: a component on a trace (complementor between its red target and black target), two empty rooms joined by a door, a via down to the trace, and a lower room
expect: recolours>=1
proof: not proved; no other solution found in 300 s
